similar in some ways to {class IO}[https://docs.ruby-lang.org/en/master/IO.html].;To;	;[I"/You can create a \StringIO instance using:;To:RDoc::Markup::List:
@type:BULLET:@items[o:RDoc::Markup::ListItem:@label0;[o;	;[I"NStringIO.new: returns a new \StringIO object containing the given string.;To;;0;[o;	;[I"EStringIO.open: passes a new \StringIO object to the given block.;To;	;[I"CLike an \IO stream, a \StringIO stream has certain properties:;To;
;;;[o;;0;[o;	;[I"ê<b>Read/write mode</b>: whether the stream may be read, written, appended to, etc.;
 see {Read/Write Mode}[rdoc-ref:StringIO@Read-2FWrite+Mode].;To;;0;[o;	;[I"Z<b>Data mode</b>: text-only or binary;
 see {Data Mode}[rdoc-ref:StringIO@Data+Mode].;To;;0;[o;	;[I"a*Encodings*: internal and external encodings;
 see {Encodings}[rdoc-ref:StringIO@Encodings].;To;;0;[o;	;[I"u*Position*: where in the stream the next read or write is to occur;
 see {Position}[rdoc-ref:StringIO@Position].;To;;0;[o;	;[I"ö<b>Line number</b>: a special, line-oriented, "position" (different from the position mentioned above);
 see {Line Number}[rdoc-ref:StringIO@Line+Number].;To;;0;[o;	;[I"ë*Open/closed*: whether the stream is open or closed, for reading or writing.
 see {Open/Closed Streams}[rdoc-ref:StringIO@Open-2FClosed+Streams].;To;;0;[o;	;[I"a*BOM*: byte mark order;
 see {Byte Order Mark}[rdoc-ref:StringIO@BOM+-28Byte+Order+Mark-29].;To:RDoc::Markup::Heading:@leveli:
